      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation first makes a dense feature field, then partitions that field into window tokens without dropping the carrier.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution image into a feature field, not a single compact vector. The symbol F names that dense carrier after encoding. The window operator partitions the carrier into tokens for processing. The symbol X names the windowed tokens while every token still comes from the dense field.",
